# Orrery — Game state

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The build owns the shape of the game's state entirely. Choose the types, the
fields, and the modules that hold them to suit the implementation you write.

The one contract fixed over the state is the debugging and automation surface
specified for this build. Every operation that surface carries is a read or a
pose of the running game, so the state holds what those operations read,
honors what they write, and returns to its title-screen values when the
surface's `reset` is called. Beyond satisfying that surface, how the state is
organized is yours to decide.

Whatever its shape, the state carries the following, because the rest of this
specification is written against them:

- The screen being shown, of `title`, `howto`, `select`, and `editor`, the
  mode the select and editor screens serve, the highlighted item of whichever
  menu is showing, the highlighted row of the select screen, and the how-to's
  current page, which the snapshot reports as `howtoPage`.
- Per-mode progress: how many campaign challenges are unlocked, which
  challenges of each mode are solved, each challenge's records, the machine
  stashed for each challenge the session has touched, and for each mode the
  challenge most recently entered or solved, which is where its select screen
  lands.
- The challenge open in the editor, if any: its full definition in the terms
  of `specs/formats.md`, and which mode and index it came from, or that it
  was loaded directly.
- The machine being edited: every placed part with its kind, pose, length,
  track path, rise or set index, and tape, exactly the facts a solution in
  `specs/formats.md` records, plus a counter that gives each new part a
  fresh identity.
- The editor's working state: the selected part, the focus, the tape cursor,
  the live drag or lay with its targeted hex, the machine as it stood at the
  press, and, for a move, the hex the press grabbed and the ghost's live
  rotation and length, and the undo and redo histories of `specs/editor.md`.
- The run, when one is active: its status, the completed-cycle count, the
  fraction through the current cycle, the speed step, every mote with its
  identity, hex, type, and whether it is a fixture of a wheel, every
  filament with its weight, every arm's live pose, every grip joining a
  gripper to a mote, each set's tally, the area bank, the fault if one was
  raised, and the metrics once complete.
- The pointer position, in the stage's logical units, and whether the
  pointer is currently pressed, both refreshed from the runtime layer in
  every update.
- The simulation time, in seconds, which every update adds its `dt` to
  whatever the screen. The snapshot reports it as `simTime`.
- The runtime's mute bit, mirrored into the state every update and reported
  by the snapshot as `muted`.
- Whether a boundary that satisfies every set's target completes the run,
  which is on while the game is played and which the surface of
  `specs/instrumentation.md` sets. The snapshot reports it as `completion`.
- Whether the frame loop advances the simulation from the wall clock, which
  is on while the game is played and which that same surface sets. The
  snapshot reports it as `autoStep`.

Progress for both modes is carried whatever the mode being played, so the
state has one shape. Fields nothing has touched yet hold their resting
values: no challenge open, an empty editor, no run, nothing solved, and only
the first campaign challenge unlocked.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
`src/game.ts` declares and exports the state the game is written against.
This section is that declaration: write it into `src/game.ts` exactly as it
stands here. The state is a value the engine holds and every frame replaces,
so every field and every array is declared `readonly`: a frame builds the
next state from the current one rather than writing into it, and every
reader is handed the state as `DeepReadonly<OrreryState>` in any case.

```ts
export type Screen = "title" | "howto" | "select" | "editor";

export type Mode = "campaign" | "extras";

export type MoteType =
  | "dust" | "nebula" | "comet" | "nova" | "meteor"
  | "mercury"
  | "saturn" | "jupiter" | "mars" | "venus" | "luna" | "sol"
  | "umbra" | "lumen" | "aether";

export type PartKind =
  | "arm" | "biarm" | "triarm" | "hexarm" | "piston" | "wheel" | "track"
  | "bind" | "manifold" | "triune" | "sunder"
  | "wane" | "mirror" | "ascend" | "conjoin" | "eclipse"
  | "confluence" | "dispersion" | "void"
  | "rise" | "set";

export type Instruction =
  | "grab" | "drop"
  | "rotate-cw" | "rotate-ccw"
  | "pivot-cw" | "pivot-ccw"
  | "extend" | "retract"
  | "advance" | "recede";

